<!-- Notification status-bar / small icon: a flat white mic-glyph silhouette
     (same Material "mic" glyph as ic_call_mic.xml — Apache 2.0,
     https://fonts.google.com/icons), not the full-colour adaptive launcher
     icon (which renders as "a logo inside the logo" once Android badges it
     onto the caller's circular Person icon, ic_launcher round-trip). A plain
     circle was tried first and had the same problem for a different reason:
     any round shape here still reads as a second sphere sitting on the
     orb's own circular silhouette — a semantically distinct glyph (a mic,
     for "voice call") reads as a badge, not a duplicate. -->
